            <ArticleTitle>Fer-ho Anaphora in Catalan: Semantic and Discourse Properties.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10936-017-9538-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper considers the anaphoric status of the pro-form fer-ho (do it) in Catalan [This paper contains some ideas included in Busquets (2005)]. I discuss some anaphoric properties of fer-ho as DEEP ANAPHORA. I also compare these properties to those of other types of anaphora, like VPE and pseudogapping (PG). I show that its interpretation is strongly constrained by information and discourse structure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
